      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    vectors = np.load('vectors.npy')  # float32, shape (8000, 1024)\n    n = vectors.shape[0]\n\n    block_size = 400\n\n    # Compute norms (sum of squares per row) in float64 for accuracy,\n    # processed in blocks to avoid large temporary allocations.\n    norms = np.empty(n, dtype=np.float64)\n    for start in range(0, n, block_size):\n        end = min(start + block_size, n)\n        blk64 = vectors[start:end].astype(np.float64)\n        norms[start:end] = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', blk64, blk64)\n        del blk64\n\n    total = 0.0\n\n    vt = vectors.T  # view, no copy\n\n    for start in range(0, n, block_size):\n        end = min(start + block_size, n)\n        block = vectors[start:end]  # float32, (b, 1024)\n\n        # float32 matmul (fast BLAS sgemm), then upcast result to float64\n        dots = block @ vt  # float32, shape (b, n)\n        dots64 = dots.astype(np.float64)\n        del dots\n\n        sq = norms[start:end][:, None] + norms[None, :] - 2.0 * dots64\n        del dots64\n\n        np.maximum(sq, 0.0, out=sq)\n        np.sqrt(sq, out=sq)\n\n        total += sq.sum()\n        del sq\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
